  "agent": "holmes-native",
  "artifact_text": "### Observations\n1. Pod logs from `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf` show recurring `WARN db connection reset by peer, retrying (pool acquire 2.80s)` errors (pod log `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf`).\n2. Deployment log `CI-2452` shows `idleClientTimeout` on `billing-db-proxy` was lowered from 1800s to 600s.\n3. The `billing-api` deployment manifest configures `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` to 900s (`billing-api` deployment spec).\n\n### Ruled-Out Leads\n1. Pod memory pressure is a symptom of request retries holding memory rather than an application leak (`INC-2024-0312`, `RB-014`).\n2. Load balancer idle timeout changes from `CI-2455` matched the HTTP keep-alive settings and did not affect database connections (`CI-2455`).\n\n### Root Cause\nRDS Proxy drops idle connections after 600s before the application pool recycles them after 900s, causing connection pool exhaustion (`RB-014`, `CI-2452`).\n\n### Recommended Action\nThe infrastructure team must raise `idleClientTimeout` on `billing-db-proxy` above 900s or revert it to default (`RB-014`, `CI-2452`).",
